.Sh NAME
.Nm jeep-prep
.Nd prepare a Janet bundle
.
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Oo
.Fl f No \&|
.Fl "-force-deps"
.Oc
.Oo
.Fl D No \&|
.Fl "-no-deps"
.Oc
.Oo
.Fl H No \&|
.Fl "-no-hook"
.Oc
.Oo
.Fl L No \&|
.Fl "-no-label"
.Ar label
.Oc
.Oo
.Fl l No \&|
.Fl "-label"
.Ar label
.Oc
.Oo
.Ar profile
.Oc
.
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
prepares a Janet bundle.
A bundle is prepared for a given profile by installing dependencies
and running the prep
.Sy bundle hook .
.
.Ss Options
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Xo
.Fl D ,
.Fl "-no-deps"
.Xc
This skips the installation of dependencies.
In other words,
it only runs the prep
.Sy bundle hook .
.It Xo
.Fl H ,
.Fl "-no-hook"
.Xc
This skips running the prep hook.
In other words,
it only installs the dependencies for the given profile.
.It Xo
.Fl L ,
.Fl "-no-label"
.Ar label
.Xc
This skips each dependency carrying the
.Ar label .
A dependency carrying no label is still installed.
This option can be invoked multiple times,
in which case a dependency is skipped if it carries any of the
labels.
.It Xo
.Fl f ,
.Fl "-force-deps"
.Xc
This forces the installation of dependencies.
By default,
Janet will not install a dependency if it is already installed.
.It Xo
.Fl l ,
.Fl "-label"
.Ar label
.Xc
This installs only the dependencies carrying the
.Ar label .
A dependency carrying no label is not installed.
This option can be invoked multiple times,
in which case a dependency is installed if it carries any of
the labels.
If a dependency carries a label given to both
.Fl "-label"
and
.Fl "-no-label" ,
it is not installed.
.It Xo
.Ar profile
.Xc
Specifies one of the following profiles to use.
Any other value is an error,
which is reported whether or not dependencies are being installed:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Xo
.Cm system
.Xc
By default,
.Nm
will use the
.Cm system
profile.
This installs the dependencies listed under
.Ql ":dependencies"
key in the
.Sy info file .
The dependencies are installed to the
.Sy syspath .
.It Xo
.Cm build
.Xc
If the user specifies the
.Cm build
profile,
this copies into the
.Eo
.Pa ./bundle
.Ec
directory several files from the Spork library that are commonly
used at build-time:
.Pp
.Bl -bullet -offset 3n -compact
.It
build-rules.janet
.It
cc.janet
.It
cjanet.janet
.It
declare-cc.janet
.It
path.janet
.It
pm-config.janet
.It
sh.janet
.It
stream.janet
.El
.It Xo
.Cm vendor
.Xc
If the user specifies the
.Cm vendor
profile,
this vendors the dependencies listed under the
.Ql ":vendored"
key in the
.Sy info file .
.El
.El
.Pp
A
.Ar label
is read in the same way as the values given to
.Xr jeep-dep 1
and
.Xr jeep-meta 1 .
A leading colon makes a keyword,
so
.Cm :dev
is the keyword
.Ql ":dev" ,
while a bare word makes a string,
so
.Cm dev
is the string
.Ql "\(dqdev\(dq" .
The two are different labels and a
.Ar label
must be written the same way as it is written in the
.Sy info file .
Labels are only meaningful for the
.Cm system
and
.Cm vendor
profiles and it is an error to give one with the
.Cm build
profile.
.Pp
For more information about the
.Sy info file ,
the
.Sy bundle script ,
.Sy bundle hooks
and the
.Sy syspath ,
see CONCEPTS in
.Xr jeep 1 .
For more information about vendoring,
see Vendoring in
.Xr jeep-dep 1 .
.
.Sh OPERATION
.Nm
consists of a two-step workflow.
First,
dependencies are installed.
Second,
the prep
.Sy bundle hook
is run.
.Pp
The bundle author specifies each dependency using a struct.
The struct should,
at a minimum,
include the
.Ql ":name"
and
.Ql ":url"
keys.
If the struct includes a
.Ql ":paths"
key,
the dependency is not installed using the Janet’s
.Ql "bundle/install"
function.
Instead
.Nm
downloads the dependency and then copies the paths listed.
Paths can be specified as strings or as two- element array/tuples
containing a source and destination path.
The source path is relative to the root of the dependency.
The destination path is relative to the directory specified
in the
.Ql ":prefix"
(if no directory is specified,
the bundle root).
Dependencies can be added to the
.Sy info file
using
.Xr jeep-dep 1 .
.Pp
A dependency can carry any number of labels,
listed under its
.Ql ":labels"
key.
A label can be a keyword or a string,
whichever the bundle author prefers,
so long as the same form is used when the label is given to
.Nm .
Labels have no meaning to
.Nm
beyond selecting which dependencies it acts on,
so a bundle author is free to choose them.
Labels can be set using
.Xr jeep-dep 1 .
.Pp
If a dependency’s URL cannot be resolved and the
.Sy info file
includes a
.Ql ":fallbacks"
key,
.Nm
tries the alternative URLs listed in the
.Sy fallbacks file .
For more information,
see Fallbacks in
.Xr jeep 1 .
.Pp
The bundle author optionally binds a function to the prep
.Sy bundle hook
by defining a function called
.Ql "prep"
in the
.Sy bundle script .
When invoked,
the function will receive two arguments:
(1)
a table representing the bundle manifest and (2)
a string matching the name of the profile specified by the user.
.
.Sh EXAMPLES
The following examples assume an
.Sy info file
as follows:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
{:name \(dqexample\(dq
 :url \(dqhttps://example\&.org/example\(dq
 :repo \(dqgit+https://example\&.org/example\(dq

 :dependencies \(lB
   {:name \(dqdep1\(dq
    :url \(dqhttps://example\&.org/dep1\(dq}
   {:name \(dqdep2\(dq
    :url \(dqhttps://example\&.org/dep2\(dq}\(rB

 :vendored \(lB
   {:name \(dqdep3\(dq
    :url \(dqhttps://example\&.org/dep3\(dq
    :prefix \(dqbundle\(dq}
   {:name \(dqdep4\(dq
    :url \(dqhttps://example\&.org/dep4\(dq
    :prefix \(dqdeps\(dq}
   {:name \(dqdep5\(dq
    :url \(dqhttps://example\&.org/dep5\(dq
    :prefix \(dqdeps/dep5\(dq
    :labels \(lB:dev\(rB
    :paths \(lB\(dqfoo\&.janet\(dq
            \(dqLICENSE\(dq\(rB}\(rB}
.Ed
.Pp
The following command prepares the bundle using the default
.Cm system
profile.
This installs ‘dep1’ and ‘dep2’ to the global syspath.
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ jeep prep
.Ed
.Pp
The following command prepares the bundle using the
.Cm system
profile.
This installs ‘dep1’ and ‘dep2’ to
.Eo
.Pa ./_system
.Ec ,
the local syspath.
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ jeep -l prep system
.Ed
.Pp
The following command prepares the bundle using the
.Cm vendor
profile.
This installs ‘dep3’ to the
.Eo
.Pa ./bundle
.Ec
directory,
installs ‘dep4’ to the
.Eo
.Pa ./deps
.Ec
directory and copies ‘foo.janet’ and ‘LICENSE’ to the
.Eo
.Pa ./deps/dep5
.Ec
directory.
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ jeep prep vendor
.Ed
.Pp
The following command prepares the bundle using the
.Cm build
profile.
This copies the default build-time files to
.Eo
.Pa ./bundle
.Ec .
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ jeep prep build
.Ed
.Pp
The following command prepares the bundle using the
.Cm vendor
profile but skips every dependency labelled ‘dev’.
This installs ‘dep3’ and ‘dep4’ but not ‘dep5’.
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ jeep prep vendor --no-label dev
.Ed
.Pp
The following command prepares the bundle using the
.Cm vendor
profile and installs only the dependencies labelled ‘dev’.
This copies ‘foo.janet’ and ‘LICENSE’ to the
.Eo
.Pa ./deps/dep5
.Ec
directory and installs nothing else.
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ jeep prep vendor --label dev
.Ed
.
